{"level":"info","ts":1738781141.7487886,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"de2b3eb9-001e-4083-8273-5784ad7114f9","content":"Alright, I've reviewed the code in `internal/handlers/github.go`. It currently handles fetching repositories and issues. I'll need to add a new handler to process GitHub webhook events related to pull requests. This handler will:\n\n1.  **Identify relevant events:** Filter for events related to pull requests (e.g., `pull_request`, `pull_request_review`, `pull_request_review_comment`).\n2.  **Check for the `dev-team` label:** Determine if the pull request has the `dev-team` label.\n3.  **Track pull requests:** If the label is present, add the pull request to the tracking list in `internal/state/state.go`.\n4.  **Handle updates:** Update the tracking list when the pull request is closed, merged, or the `dev-team` label is removed.\n5.  **Handle comments:** When a comment is added to a tracked pull request, create a new commit to address the comment.\n\nHere's how I plan to modify the files:\n\n*   **`internal/handlers/github.go`:**\n    *   Add a new handler function `HandleGitHubPullRequestEvent(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)`.\n    *   This handler will parse the webhook payload, check the event type and label, and update the tracking list in `internal/state/state.go`.\n    *   It will also call the function to create a commit when a comment is added.\n*   **`internal/state/state.go`:**\n    *   Add a field to the `State` struct to store the tracked pull requests (e.g., `TrackedPullRequests map[string]bool`). The key will be the pull request ID.\n    *   Add methods to add, remove, and check if a pull request is being tracked.\n*   **`pkg/github/github.go`:**\n    *   Potentially add a function to create a new commit on a pull request.  I'll need to investigate the best way to do this using the GitHub API.\n*   **`pkg/repository/pullRequest.go`:**\n    *   This file might need updates if I need to fetch more information about a pull request.\n\nLet's start by modifying `internal/state/state.go` to add the tracking list.\n\n"}
