{"level":"info","ts":1738781402.7090342,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"2e4f7289-7789-4dac-a1ab-0d2406451e54","content":"Okay, I see a number of issues here. Let's break them down and address them one by one:\n\n1.  **`cmd/dev-team/main.go:11:2: could not import github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/internal/config`**: This suggests there's a problem with the `internal/config` package. It's likely related to a previous error preventing the package from being built correctly. Let's look at the `internal/config/config.go` error first.\n2.  **`internal/config/config.go:60:18: cannot use state.State.GenAI (variable of type \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider) as *\"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider value in argument to r.Sync`**: It seems the `Sync` method expects a pointer to a `genai.Provider`, but we're passing a value. We should pass `&state.State.GenAI` instead of `state.State.GenAI`.\n3.  **`cmd/dev-team/main.go:101:20: cannot use state.State.GenAI (variable of type \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider) as *\"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider value in argument to repo.Sync`**: Same issue as above, needs to be a pointer.\n4.  **`cmd/dev-team/main.go:136:23: undefined: state.Settings`**: This indicates that `state` does not have a field called `Settings`. It should be `state.State.Settings`.\n5.  **`internal/handlers/repository.go:14:2: could not import github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/internal/config`**: This should be resolved after fixing the `internal/config/config.go` error.\n6.  **`internal/handlers/gemini.go:11:26: invalid operation: state.State.GenAI == nil (mismatched types \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider and untyped nil)`**: The `GenAI` field is of type `genai.Provider`, not `*genai.Provider`, so it cannot be `nil`. To check if it's initialized, we can check if the Provider field is empty string.\n7.  **`internal/handlers/github.go:88:33: state.State.Settings.GitHubWebhookSecret undefined (type settings.Settings has no field or method GitHubWebhookSecret)`**: It seems the `GitHubWebhookSecret` field is missing from the `settings.Settings` struct. I need to add this field to `internal/settings/settings.go`.\n8.  **`internal/handlers/github.go:175:20: assignment mismatch: 2 variables but 1 value`**:  The map access `state.State.TrackedPRs` is not being checked correctly. We only need to check the existence of the map, the value doesn't matter. The correct statement is `if state.State.TrackedPRs == nil`.\n9.  **`internal/handlers/github.go:290:20: assignment mismatch: 2 variables but 1 value`**: Same problem as #8.\n10. **`internal/handlers/repository.go:72:20: cannot use state.State.GenAI (variable of type \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider) as *\"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider value in argument to repo.Sync`**: Same issue as 2 & 3.\n11. **`internal/handlers/repository.go:337:18: cannot use state.State.GenAI (variable of type \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider) as *\"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider value in argument to repo.Sync`**: Same issue as 2, 3 & 10.\n12. **`internal/handlers/settings.go:58:23: cannot use genaiProvider (variable of type *\"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider) as \"github.com/jbutlerdev/genai\".Provider value in assignment`**: In `main.go` the type of GenAI in `AppState` is not a pointer. Should assign the value directly.\n\nLet's start by fixing the `internal/settings/settings.go` file.\n\n"}
