{"level":"info","ts":1738781808.7360454,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"2fdbb6dd-baa6-490f-b2b8-f45288ff2fda","content":"Now that the `TrackedPullRequests` map is initialized, I can implement the logic for handling pull request events in `internal/handlers/github.go`. This will involve:\n\n1.  Decoding the webhook payload.\n2.  Checking the event type and extracting relevant information (e.g., pull request number, labels, state).\n3.  Updating the `TrackedPullRequests` map based on the event.\n4.  If a comment is added to a tracked pull request, creating a new commit to address it.\n\nI'll start by reading the contents of `pkg/github/github.go` to see how I can interact with the github API.\n\n"}
