{"level":"info","ts":1738783908.7479095,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"1ba3636d-8e7a-4989-af6e-e4a2ebc72679","content":"I have now implemented the logic to:\n\n*   Track pull requests with the `dev-team` label.\n*   Fetch comments for tracked pull requests.\n*   Generate a patch using the GenAI provider to address the comment.\n\nHowever, due to the limitations of the `writeFile` API, I was unable to implement the following steps:\n\n*   Clone the repository.\n*   Checkout the PR's branch.\n*   Commit the changes.\n*   Push the changes.\n\nThese steps would require the ability to execute shell commands, which is not supported by the current API.\n\nThe implemented code provides a foundation for tracking pull requests and generating patches to address comments. To fully automate the process, you would need to integrate it with a system that can execute shell commands and interact with Git.\n"}
