{"level":"info","ts":1738784413.276527,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"3e9135bd-a44b-47df-8439-6853c783528a","content":"Okay, I have addressed the syntax error in `pkg/github/github.go` and resolved the import cycle between `internal/config` and `internal/state`. I have also updated the code to pass the GitHub token correctly. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n*   **`pkg/github/github.go`:** Fixed the syntax error and rewrote the `AddCommitToPullRequest` function to correctly add a commit that addresses the comment to the pull request.\n*   **`internal/state/state.go`:** Removed the import of `internal/config` and added a `GitHubToken` field to the `StateData` struct.\n*   **`internal/config/config.go`:** Removed the import of `internal/state` and modified the `LoadConfig` function to return the repositories, settings, and scheduler separately.\n*   **`cmd/dev-team/main.go`:** Modified the `main` function to reflect the changes in `internal/config/config.go` and pass the necessary configuration values to the `state` package.\n*   **`internal/handlers/github.go`:** Modified the `HandleGitHubPullRequest` function to pass the GitHub token to the `AddCommitToPullRequest` function.\n\nThese changes should address the identified issues and implement the requested functionality for tracking pull requests with the `dev-team` label and adding commits to address comments.\n"}
