{"level":"info","ts":1738786544.0299325,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"0e8b7532-e326-4943-84b2-3cf914eedb3d","content":"Okay, I see several issues.\n\n1.  **Import cycle:** There's an import cycle between `internal/config` and `internal/state`. This needs to be resolved by restructuring the dependencies. The `internal/state` package shouldn't depend on `internal/config`. Instead, the necessary configuration values should be passed to functions in `internal/state` as arguments.\n2.  **Incorrect function calls:** The `client.Git.CreateCommit` function requires an additional argument of type `*github.CreateCommitOptions`.\n3.  **Undefined functions:** The functions `github.FetchRepositories`, `github.ValidateWebhook`, and `github.AddCommitToPullRequest` are not being properly called due to the package name collision with `github.com/google/go-github/v57/github`.\n\nHere's how I'll address these issues:\n\n1.  **Resolve import cycle:** I'll remove the import of `internal/config` from `internal/state/state.go` and pass the necessary configuration values (e.g., GitHub token, webhook secret) as arguments to functions that need them.\n2.  **Correct function calls:** I'll update the call to `client.Git.CreateCommit` in `pkg/github/github.go` to include the `*github.CreateCommitOptions` argument. I'll use `context.Background()` as the context for this argument.\n3.  **Fix package name collision:**  I will rename the import `github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/pkg/github` to `internalgithub` to avoid conflicts with `github.com/google/go-github/v57/github`.  Then, I will update the code to call the functions using the new alias.\n\nLet's start by fixing the import cycle in `internal/state/state.go`.\n\n"}
