{"level":"info","ts":1738786571.6100752,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"0e8b7532-e326-4943-84b2-3cf914eedb3d","content":"Okay, I see a few remaining issues:\n\n1.  **Unused import:** The `internalgithub` package is imported but not used in several files in the `pkg/repository` directory.\n2.  **Undefined github:** There are still references to the `github` package in the `pkg/repository` directory, which should now be `internalgithub`.\n3.  **Import errors:** The `internal/state/state.go`, `cmd/dev-team/main.go`, and `internal/config/config.go` files are having trouble importing `github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/pkg/repository`.\n4.  **Undefined github in internal/handlers/repository.go:** There's a reference to `github.CreateDraftPR` which should now be `internalgithub.CreateDraftPR`.\n\nHere's the plan to address these:\n\n1.  **Modify `pkg/repository` files:** Update the files in `pkg/repository` to use `internalgithub` where appropriate and remove the import if it's not used.\n2.  **Modify `internal/handlers/repository.go`:** Use `internalgithub.CreateDraftPR` instead of `github.CreateDraftPR`.\n3.  **Investigate import errors:** Examine the `internal/state/state.go`, `cmd/dev-team/main.go`, and `internal/config/config.go` to determine why they are having issues importing `github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/pkg/repository` and fix them.\n\nLet's start by modifying the files in `pkg/repository`. I'll start with `pkg/repository/issue.go`.\n\n"}
