{"level":"info","ts":1738788350.265433,"logger":"repository","caller":"repository/repository.go:329","msg":"Response","path":"/data/jbutler/tmpgit/jbutlerdev/dev-team","response":"OK, I've updated the `HandleGitHubPullRequests` function in `internal/handlers/github.go` to store the fetched pull requests in the `TrackedPullRequests` map in the application state.\n\nNow, we need to implement the logic to track the status of the pull requests and remove them from the `TrackedPullRequests` map when they are closed, merged, or the `dev-team` label is removed.\n\nI'll start by creating a function that checks the status of the tracked pull requests and updates the `TrackedPullRequests` map accordingly. This function will be called periodically by the scheduler.\n\nI'll add this function to `internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`. First, let's read the file.\n\n"}
