{"level":"info","ts":1738790108.1749473,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"f0e4df98-87d8-41d1-b741-37a3ae436f38","content":"Okay, I see that `internal/handlers/github.go` currently handles fetching repositories and issues. It doesn't seem to have any logic for handling webhook events. I'll need to add a new handler function to handle GitHub webhook events. This handler will need to:\n\n1.  Determine the event type from the `X-GitHub-Event` header.\n2.  Parse the event payload.\n3.  If the event is related to a pull request (e.g., `pull_request`, `pull_request_review_comment`, `issues` with label changes), check if the pull request has the `dev-team` label.\n4.  If the pull request has the `dev-team` label, track it.\n5.  If the pull request is closed, merged, or the `dev-team` label is removed, stop tracking it.\n6.  If a comment is added to a tracked pull request, add a new commit to the pull request.\n\nI'll also need to modify `internal/state/state.go` to store the tracked pull requests and provide methods for adding, removing, and checking if a pull request is being tracked.\n\nLet's start by modifying `internal/state/state.go` to add the pull request tracking functionality.\n\n"}
