{"level":"info","ts":1738790125.9119432,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"f0e4df98-87d8-41d1-b741-37a3ae436f38","content":"Okay, I've implemented the pull request tracking logic in `internal/handlers/github.go`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n*   Added a `HandleGitHubWebhook` function to handle GitHub webhook events.\n*   The `HandleGitHubWebhook` function determines the event type from the `X-GitHub-Event` header and parses the event payload.\n*   Added helper functions `handlePullRequestEvent`, `handlePullRequestReviewCommentEvent`, and `handleIssuesEvent` to handle specific event types.\n*   The `handlePullRequestEvent` function tracks pull requests with the `dev-team` label when they are opened, reopened, labeled, or synchronized. It also untracks pull requests when they are closed.\n*   The `handlePullRequestReviewCommentEvent` function adds a new commit to the pull request when a comment is added to a tracked pull request. (This is currently a placeholder and needs to be implemented.)\n*   The `handleIssuesEvent` function tracks pull requests with the `dev-team` label when the label is added and untracks them when the label is removed or the issue is closed.\n*   Modified `internal/state/state.go` to include a map of tracked pull requests and methods for tracking and untracking pull requests.\n\nThe next step is to implement the logic to add a new commit to the pull request when a comment is added to a tracked pull request. This will involve using the GitHub API to create a new commit on the pull request's branch. I'll need to read the `pkg/github/github.go` file to see how the GitHub API is currently being used and add a new function to create a commit.\n\n"}
