{"level":"info","ts":1738791916.8678343,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash-exp","id":"41093767-cbeb-48b2-88c0-371cd64079bf","content":"This file defines the `AppState` struct, which holds the application's state, including repositories, settings, and the scheduler. It seems like a good place to store the list of tracked pull requests. We'll add a new field to `AppState` to store this information.\n\nNow we have enough information to start implementing the changes. Here's the proposed implementation:\n\n1.  **Modify `internal/state/state.go`:**\n    *   Add a new field `TrackedPullRequests` to the `AppState` struct. This field will be a map where the key is the URL of the pull request and the value is a boolean indicating whether the PR is currently being tracked.\n\n2.  **Modify `pkg/github/github.go`:**\n    *   Modify the `FetchPullRequests` function to accept an additional `label` argument.\n    *   Filter the pull requests based on the provided `label`. Only pull requests with the specified label should be returned.\n\n3.  **Modify `internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`:**\n    *   In the scheduled task, fetch pull requests using the modified `FetchPullRequests` function, passing the `dev-team` label.\n    *   Iterate through the fetched pull requests:\n        *   If a pull request is not already tracked (i.e., not in `TrackedPullRequests`), add it to `TrackedPullRequests`.\n        *   If a pull request is already tracked, check if it has been closed, merged, or if the `dev-team` label has been removed. If any of these conditions are true, remove it from `TrackedPullRequests`.\n        *   Check if a new comment has been added to the pull request. If so, add a new commit to the pull request that addresses the comment.\n\n4.  **Modify `internal/config/config.go`:**\n    *   Update the `LoadConfig` and `SaveConfig` to handle the new `TrackedPullRequests` field in `AppState`.\n\nLet's start by modifying `internal/state/state.go`.\n\n"}
