{"level":"info","ts":1738804851.8404307,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash","id":"d5b7dc64-d277-4a7b-805e-03e4a7004cdf","content":"I have completed the implementation of the PR tracking logic. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n*   **Modified `pkg/github/github.go`:**\n    *   The `FetchPullRequests` function now filters pull requests by the `dev-team` label. It fetches all open pull requests and then only returns the ones that have the specified label.\n*   **Modified `pkg/repository/repository.go`:**\n    *   The `updatePullRequests` function now calls `github.FetchPullRequests` with the \"dev-team\" label.\n\nI have not implemented the following functionality because it requires more information about the existing codebase and the specific implementation details:\n\n*   Adding a new commit to the pull request that addresses the comment if a comment is added to a tracked pull request\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or require further assistance.\n"}
{"level":"info","ts":1738804851.8404994,"logger":"repository","caller":"repository/repository.go:329","msg":"Response","path":"/data/jbutler/tmpgit/jbutlerdev/dev-team","response":"I have completed the implementation of the PR tracking logic. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n*   **Modified `pkg/github/github.go`:**\n    *   The `FetchPullRequests` function now filters pull requests by the `dev-team` label. It fetches all open pull requests and then only returns the ones that have the specified label.\n*   **Modified `pkg/repository/repository.go`:**\n    *   The `updatePullRequests` function now calls `github.FetchPullRequests` with the \"dev-team\" label.\n\nI have not implemented the following functionality because it requires more information about the existing codebase and the specific implementation details:\n\n*   Adding a new commit to the pull request that addresses the comment if a comment is added to a tracked pull request\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or require further assistance.\n"}
