{"level":"info","ts":1738806312.4405708,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/gemini.go:78","msg":"Handling text","model":"models/gemini-2.0-flash","id":"dc3c6018-7dad-400f-9beb-fd2c78f37eef","content":"Okay, this file defines the `Repository` struct and several methods for interacting with a Git repository, including cloning, committing, pushing, fetching, and syncing.\n\nThe `Sync` method is the most relevant here. It calls `UpdatePullRequests` and `UpdateIssues` to get the latest data from GitHub. It also contains the logic for creating a branch, generating changes using an AI service, and creating a pull request.\n\nNow let's look at `pkg/repository/pullRequest.go` and `pkg/repository/issue.go` to see how pull requests and issues are represented and updated. This will help us understand how to access PR comments.\n\n"}
