{"level":"info","ts":1738893855.6970851,"logger":"genai-provider.chat","caller":"genai/ollama.go:124","msg":"Handling text","model":"qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q6_K","id":"546d7baf-c445-44e8-8f96-829d3a0fbd19","content":"Based on the file structure provided, it looks like your codebase is primarily in Go. The `pullRequest.go` and `repository.go` files under the `internal/pkg/repository` directory might be relevant for handling pull requests.\n\nLet's start by writing a function to address comments from PRs that are associated with dev-team issues. We'll use the existing polling logic as instructed.\n\nHere is an example of how you can write this code:\n\n```go\npackage repository\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\n\t\"github.com/jbutlerdev/dev-team/internal/pkg/polling\" // Adjust import if needed based on your actual import path\n)\n\nfunc AddressPRComments() {\n\t// Get all open pull requests associated with dev-team issues.\n\tpullRequests, err := polling.GetOpenPullRequests()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Error fetching pull requests: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tfor _, pr := range pullRequests {\n\t\t// Fetch comments on the PR.\n\t\tprComments, err := polling.GetPRComments(pr.Number)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Error fetching comments for PR #%d: %v\\n\", pr.Number, err)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Process each comment.\n\t\tfor _, comment := range prComments {\n\t\t\t// Pass the comment to a model as a prompt.\n\t\t\tprompt := fmt.Sprintf(\"Address the following comment from pull request #{}: {}\", pr.Number, comment.Body)\n\n\t\t\t// Get the response from the model.\n\t\t\tresponse, err := GenerateModelResponse(prompt)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Printf(\"Error generating response for comment in PR #{}: %v\\n\", pr.Number, err)\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Create a new commit with the addressed comment.\n\t\t\tcommitMessage := fmt.Sprintf(\"Addressed feedback from comment on PR #%d\", pr.Number)\n\t\t\tif err 